<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Automation on behaviorengineering.ai</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/tags/automation/</link><description>Recent content in Automation on behaviorengineering.ai</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 01:00:00 +1100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/tags/automation/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>🦑🧠 You think you think?</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/human-condition/2026-06-25-ai-thinking-planes-octopus/</link><pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/human-condition/2026-06-25-ai-thinking-planes-octopus/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;People say AI is &lt;strong&gt;taking our thinking&lt;/strong&gt;. That is partly right. It may only be right on the &lt;strong&gt;habit plane&lt;/strong&gt;. We still have to think; we just have to do it on the &lt;strong&gt;metacognition plane&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="when-thinking-is-someone-elses-script"&gt;When &amp;ldquo;thinking&amp;rdquo; is someone else&amp;rsquo;s script&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A lot of what we call thinking right now is &lt;strong&gt;following someone else&amp;rsquo;s thinking&lt;/strong&gt; without giving it real thought. Opinions arrive pre-packaged. Reactions fire before you ask why. Mental habits run like &lt;strong&gt;muscle memory&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Predictability is exactly what you automate first</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-23-tshirt-predictability-automates-first/</link><pubDate>Sat, 23 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-23-tshirt-predictability-automates-first/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Commute for the culture</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-07-cow-w11/</link><pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-07-cow-w11/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Clear the loops, keep the stop</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-04-22-tshirt-stop-button/</link><pubDate>Wed, 22 Apr 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-10/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-04-22-tshirt-stop-button/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>